# Frontend Module Conventions

## API calls

All HTTP calls for a feature belong in that module's `domain/api.ts` file.
Use the shared Axios instance from `src/api/axios.ts` — do not create a second instance.

```
src/modules/<name>/domain/api.ts   ← HTTP calls go here
```

Hooks may wrap `domain/api.ts` calls to manage local state. That is the expected pattern.
Direct HTTP calls inside components (outside a hook or `domain/api.ts`) are not the established convention.

## Secure document access

For PDFs, payroll documents, sick-leave attachments, and any file served from `/api/files/`:
use `openSecureFile()` from `src/utils/openSecureFile.ts`.

The security policy behind this (public `/uploads` vs authenticated `/api/files/`) is in `CLAUDE.md`.

## Locale sync

When adding any user-visible string, add the translation key to all three locale files:
- `src/locales/de/translation.json`
- `src/locales/en/translation.json`
- `src/locales/es/translation.json`

All three files must stay in sync. A key missing from one locale will silently fall back or display the key name.

## Shared UI primitives

Before creating a new button or action component, check `src/components/common/`:
- `actions/` — Save, Cancel, Create, Edit, Delete, DangerDelete, DayOff
- `PageShell.tsx` — standard page wrapper
- `StatusBadge.tsx` — status pill
- `FileUpload.tsx` — upload widget
